From ba3de813c7295c02697bb59b41624c9ec89856c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:01:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 046/638] gpu: exclude Ozone pixmap backings on AROS

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell

AI_STATUS: The AROS GPU service now builds and registers shared-memory image backings without compiling Ozone's NativePixmap-specific backing family.

ROOT_CAUSE: Patch 0028 removed native pixmap handles from AROS GpuMemoryBufferHandle, but gpu/command_buffer/service still compiled OzoneImageBacking and its GL, Vulkan, and Dawn representations and registered OzoneImageBackingFactory.

FIX_REASON: Exclude only the NativePixmap-specific Ozone backing sources and factory on AROS while retaining Ozone platform integration, shared-memory image factories, EGL/ANGLE paths, and future non-pixmap acceleration work.

SCOPE: gpu command-buffer service GN source graph and SharedImageFactory registration

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j16 obj/gpu/command_buffer/service/libgles2_sources.a passed; regenerated Ninja graph contains shared_memory_image_backing objects and no OzoneImageBacking objects; git diff --check passed.

RISK: NativePixmap zero-copy import, accelerated scanout, and its Vulkan/Dawn representations remain unavailable until AROS defines native image handles and synchronization.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn                         | 6 +++---
 .../service/shared_image/shared_image_factory.cc            | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

